`compat <old> <new>` (#612, FJ4): two contract revisions, judged by the
contract CI's own classifier (spec §9.8) — `zenkey_model::compat`, the one
`zk2 contract compat` and the codegen's history gate run — so the tool cannot
disagree with the build about what breaks.

A side is an authoring file (`*.toml`), a bundle file (`*.bundle.json`,
verified against its own content), or `<iface>[@<fingerprint>]`: a revision
`--contracts` holds or the deployment's descriptors name. A verdict verb, on
the one contract in `zenctl/src/exit.rs`: **0** compatible, **1** review or
breaking (the finding), **2** no verdict.

None of these opens a session: every side is a file or held by `--contracts`.

The published revision of `tc.netif.v1` against its own authoring file: the
same fingerprint, and compatible.

```console
$ zenctl compat ../examples/zk2/.history/tc.netif.v1/4f531ebec4c4eee015c18f11aefbce9138b413cfdca6bf6b777ea0eb6f43b4e0.bundle.json ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml --format table
old  tc.netif.v1  sha256:4f531ebec4c4eee0…  bundle  ../examples/zk2/.history/tc.netif.v1/4f531ebec4c4eee015c18f11aefbce9138b413cfdca6bf6b777ea0eb6f43b4e0.bundle.json
new  tc.netif.v1  sha256:4f531ebec4c4eee0…  file    ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml

compatible
0 finding(s), 0 warning(s); exit 0.

```

A review change — the bandwidth stream's cardinality doubled — is a finding a
human accepts, exit 1:

```console
$ zenctl compat ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2/review/tc.netif.v1.toml --format table
? 1
old  tc.netif.v1  sha256:4f531ebec4c4eee0…  file  ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
new  tc.netif.v1  sha256:94b92cc2ff1b030a…  file  tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2/review/tc.netif.v1.toml

review  cardinality_changed  resources."bandwidth/{ns}/{iface}"
  `cardinality` changed

review
1 finding(s), 0 warning(s); exit 1: a human accepts a review change.

```

A breaking one, with the old side named by interface and a fingerprint prefix
out of `--contracts` — a `.history` root, the published bundles:

```console
$ zenctl compat tc.netif.v1@4f53 tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2/breaking/tc.netif.v1.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/.history --format table
? 1
old  tc.netif.v1  sha256:4f531ebec4c4eee0…  history  tc.netif.v1@4f53
new  tc.netif.v1  sha256:05e9f1168915c594…  file     tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2/breaking/tc.netif.v1.toml

breaking  resource_removed  resources."namespaces"
  removed; a deprecated resource stays until the next major

breaking
1 finding(s), 0 warning(s); exit 1: a breaking change needs a new major.

```

Two different interfaces are breaking by definition, and the report says so
rather than listing every resource as removed:

```console
$ zenctl compat ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netem.v1.toml --format table
? 1
old  tc.netif.v1  sha256:4f531ebec4c4eee0…  file  ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
new  tc.netem.v1  sha256:30b491116ef6a534…  file  ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netem.v1.toml

breaking  interface_changed  interface
  the interface id differs

breaking
1 finding(s), 0 warning(s); exit 1: a breaking change needs a new major.
the two revisions are of different interfaces (tc.netif.v1 and tc.netem.v1): that alone is breaking

```

## No verdict

An input that cannot be read is no verdict on compatibility — exit 2, never
the 1 that would read as "breaking":

```console
$ zenctl compat tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2/missing.toml ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2/missing.toml: no such file
compat: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

A revision `--contracts` does not hold has to be retrieved from the bus — and
a bus that cannot be reached asked nothing:

```console
$ zenctl compat tc.netif.v1@ffff ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/.history --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!
compat: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```
